{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"vegetarian-mica-phoebe","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`src/rebar/llm/evals/engine_comparison.py` (antifungal-amenable-mite, Gerrit 3366, merged 73848dd1f40) has 3 defects that affect the numbers it records. All 3 were confirmed against the committed `src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/engine_comparison_results.json`:\n\n1. **Overlap undercounts pipeline findings.** `_surfaced` reads only `blocking` + `advisory`. The verdict's `advisory` list is already cut at `orchestrator.DEFAULT_ADVISORY_CAP` (20), and DET advisories count toward that cap; `overflow` is never read. In the recorded run, 3 of 11 rows have exactly 19 non-DET pipeline findings, which is the cap minus the DET advisory. So `pipeline_only` and every overlap total are understated, and each row's count depends on the cap.\n2. **`--resume` mixes stale records.** `main` loads `--out` and `run()` reuses its items by `review_event_uuid` without checking that the saved `corpus_digest`, `corpus` and `match_threshold` match the current run. A changed labels file, `--limit` or threshold silently mixes old per-item records into new results.\n3. **No model or runner is recorded.** `_review_in_fresh_store` drops the verdict that carries `runner`/`model`, so the results cannot say which models produced them. The recorded run used the Anthropic API config while the docs show the Bedrock command, and the file cannot show the difference.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Overlap reads `blocking` + `advisory` + `overflow` (non-DET), pinned by a test with more than 20 pipeline advisories.\n- [ ] `--resume` refuses (exit 2, message names the mismatched field) when the saved digest, corpus or threshold differs, pinned by a test.\n- [ ] Each per-engine record carries the verdict's `runner` and `model`, pinned by a test.\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0.","id":"e1f6-d986-5adc-4d0b","parent_id":"9794-4336-5ed6-4561","priority":3,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Engine comparison undercounts pipeline findings, mixes stale resume records, and records no model"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1794530512856650016,"uuid":"11f14638-4d63-41f5-b72d-0e2ea1cb6b98"}